my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
alpha beta alpha gamma alpha
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{N after backward search goes forward},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/search_N_after_backward`

After a **?pattern** backward search, **N** repeats in the opposite direction (forward). `?alpha` from the end finds the last "alpha", then `N` goes forward to the next one.

**Keys:** `$` then `?alpha\n` then `N`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0
- Three "alpha" occurrences on the line

**after_move_to_end.png**
- Cursor at end of line, col 30

**after_backward_search.png**
- Cursor on last "alpha" at col 23 (searched backward from end)

**after_N_forward.png**
- Cursor on the "alpha" at col 12 (moved forward from last match)
- `N` reversed the backward search direction
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('$');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_to_end');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('?alpha\n');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_backward_search');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('N');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_N_forward');
    },
}
